,title,link,text,language,family
0,Anuak language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anuak_language,Anuak or Anywaa is a Luo language which belongs to the western Nilotic branch of the Nilotic language family. It is spoken primarily in the western part of Ethiopia and also in South Sudan by the Anuak people.,Anuak,Nilo-Saharan
1,Male Singers Using Other Nilo-Saharan... - Ethiopian Gospel Music,https://ethiopiangospelmusic.net/vignettes/other-nilo-saharan/,Anywaa (aka Anuak). Aballa Agwa. Deng Ojulu.Cookie policy (EU). Disclaimer. Ethiopian Gospel Music.,Anuak,Nilo-Saharan
2,What Are Nilotic People in Ethiopia Known For?,https://www.ethiopiaimmigration.org/faq/what-are-nilotic-people-in-ethiopia-known-for,"Languages: They speak Nilotic languages, which belong to the Nilo-Saharan family. Religion: The religions include Christianity, Islam, and traditional religions. Arts and traditions: Music, dance, and oral storytelling play important roles in preserving cultural heritage.",Anuak,Nilo-Saharan
3,Anuak in South Sudan people group profile | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/people_groups/10354/od,"The Anuak speak a Nilotic language known as Anuak. Unlike other Nilotic people in the region whose economy is centered on raising cattle, the Anuak are mainly farmers. They probably have a common origin with their northern neighbors, the Shilluk.Nilo-Saharan.",Anuak,Nilo-Saharan
4,Anuak - anu (Nilo-Saharan) - PeopleGroups.org,https://peoplegroups.org/language/anu/,"Anuak (anu) is part of the Nilo-Saharan family and Nilo-Saharan, Satellite-Core, Core, Eastern Sudanic, Southern (n languages), Nilotic, Western, Luo, Northern, Anuak class. Anuak speaking People Groups across the world: Fast Facts: Types.",Anuak,Nilo-Saharan
5,Anuak (Dha-Anywaa) — 20 words & pronunciations | Word Map,https://langmap.heuron.com/en/wordmap/anu,"Nilo-Saharan.Linguistically, Anuak shares Lwoo Western Nilotic features with sister languages Acholi (ach), Lango (laj), and Luo (luo) — including ATR vowel harmony with two harmonic sets, a complex tone system (typically 3-4 tone register), and verbal aspect-mood morphology.",Anuak,Nilo-Saharan
6,(PDF) Nilo-Saharan Languages,https://www.researchgate.net/publication/304040925_Nilo-Saharan_Languages,"Nilo-Saharan is essentially Greenberg's earlier Macro-Sudanic (or Chari-Nile) family, together with languages and language groups formerly assigned to historically isolated units.Western. Burun. Shilluk, Anuak, Acholi, Lango, Alur, Luo, Jur, Bor. Dinka, Nuer.",Anuak,Nilo-Saharan
7,Exploring The Anuak Language: A Journey Into The Heart Of...,https://languagexs.com/anuak-language/,"Anuak, also known as Anywa or Dha-Anywaa, is a Nilo-Saharan language spoken by the Anuak people. It is a language of great linguistic interest due to its unique phonetic and grammatical features.Comparative Study: Anuak and Other Nilo-Saharan Languages.",Anuak,Nilo-Saharan
8,Anuak Language Sample | Language Museum,https://www.language-museum.com/encyclopedia/a/anuak.php,"If you want to get a flavour of the Anuak language, check out a small sample at the Language Museum.Sudan (52,000) - Ethiopia (26,000) - Total (78,000). Classification. Nilo-Saharan | Eastern Sudanic.",Anuak,Nilo-Saharan
9,Nilo-Saharan | Ethnologue Free,https://www.ethnologue.com/subgroup/39/?cf=1&token=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..q1Sf4rd3drUq_qVbZh2jE_3soRxTIxU8lmX0apb_0eA,"Nilo-Saharan. Subgroup of 210 languages.Anuak anu, a language of South Sudan.",Anuak,Nilo-Saharan
